    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "A total of 500 mg of Arabidopsis leaves from plants growing under NPC and APC for 3 days were grounded in liquid nitrogen and total protein extract was prepared in PBS, pH 8, supplemented with 1% protease inhibitor (cOmplete™, SigmaAldrich) and 2% SDS, then it was incubated with 5 mM 4-chloro-7-nitrobenzofurazan (Cl-NBF, SigmaAldrich) at 37 ºC for 30 min, protected from light. To eliminate excess Cl-NBF, a methanol/chloroform precipitation was performed, and protein pellets obtained were washed with cold methanol, dried and dissolved in 50 mM sodium phosphate, pH 8, with 2% SDS, as described previously [17,18]. Proteins were then incubated with 100 µM DCP-Bio1 (Merck) at 37 ºC for 2h. Afterwards, proteins were precipitated with methanol/chloroform and dissolved in PBS supplemented with 0.1% SDS. Proteins were incubated with Sera-Mag™ Magnetic Streptavidin (Cytiva) at 4 ºC overnight with agitation and then, beads were washed with 8 column volumes of PBS, pH 8, with 0.001% Tween, 2 column volumes of PBS, pH 8, and 1 column volume of pure HPLC-quality water. After washing, beads were incubated 5h with agitation with 2.25 M ammonium hydroxide at RT. The sample was then neutralized with formic acid and protein concentration was determined.Proteins were redesolved in 50mM Ammonium bicarbonate and samples were digested with 1:20 ratio Trypsin (Promega, V5111): proteins.Peptides were dissolved in 0.1% TFA before being analyzed by high-resolution LC-MS/MS using an Ultimate 3000 Nano Ultra High-Pressure Chromatography (UPLC) system (Thermo Fisher Scientific) coupled with an Orbitrap Lumos™ Tribrid™ Mass Spectrometer via an EASY-spray (Thermo Fisher Scientific). Peptide separation was carried out with an Acclaim™ PepMap™ 100 C18 column (Thermo Fisher Scientific) using a 60min gradient (0 min, 7% B; 19 min, 10% B; 56 min, 20% B; 74 min, 30% B;  B: 84% Acetonitrile, 0.1% Formic Acid) at a flow rate of 250 nL/min. The Orbitrap Eclipse™ was operated in a DDA mode and MS1 survey scans were acquired from m/z 300 to 1,800 at a resolution of 120, 000 using the Orbitrap mode. The most intense ions were isolated for 3 seconds with a 1 m/z window and then fragmented by high-energy collision-induced dissociation (HCD) with a normalized collision energy of 28%, considering a dynamic exclusion of 20 s. MS/MS spectra were recorded using Orbitrap mode with a resolution of 30, 000.",
